module
public import Causalean.Stat.CLT.BerryEsseen.PrawitzRationalArithmetic

/-! # Exact rational grid data for compact Prawitz budgets

The parameter grid has ninety cells of width 1/1000 on [1/100,1/10]
and one hundred eighty cells of width 1/200 on [1/10,1]. Low frequency
cells have width 1/200, and high cells have width 1/1000 in the kernel
variable. All tables are explicit integers. Their entries and finite sums
are obligations in the three separate certificate modules, not assumptions.

Sixteen-term reciprocal Taylor bounds replace negative exponentials.
Each cell bound is rounded UP to one hundred millionth before summation;
this keeps denominators small without relying on approximate arithmetic.
The singular low cell [0,1/200] uses its proved polynomial integral bound.
The high sum includes every cell from its lower integer index through 999;
the analytic comparison at the assigned kernel endpoint is only a.e.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Causalean.Stat.CLT.BerryEsseen

open Finset

/-- The [left endpoint](goal) of [the j-th parameter cell](hyp:j) is
(10 + j)/1000 for j < 90 and (20 + (j − 90))/200 for j ≥ 90: the cells have
width one thousandth from 1/100 up to 1/10 and width one two hundredth from
1/10 onward. -/
def prawitzCompactLeft (j : ℕ) : ℚ :=
  if j < 90 then (10 + (j : ℚ)) / 1000 else (20 + ((j - 90 : ℕ) : ℚ)) / 200

/-- The [right endpoint](goal) of [the j-th parameter cell](hyp:j) is the
left endpoint of cell j + 1, so consecutive cells have no gaps. -/
def prawitzCompactRight (j : ℕ) : ℚ := prawitzCompactLeft (j + 1)

